  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1007 PM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nA subtle shift in the upper pattern begins early next week as the\nridge axis starts to drift to the SW. This should allow for some\nsubtle cooling, beginning Monday across the northern portions of \nthe area and expanding SW by Tuesday. Highs will still remain in \nthe mid 90s early week, but the humidity will be lower. Overnight \nlows remain in the 70s.\n\nLow chances of afternoon/evening showers and storms return next\nweek, driven by afternoon instability and any weak impulses that\ncan sneak around the ridge. Coverage is expected to remain\nisolated to scattered at best. \n\nThrough the middle of the week, temperatures stay above normal\nunder continued ridging influence, though not quite as oppressive\nas the weekend peak. Daily highs mostly in the upper to mid 90s \nwith heat indices still frequently reaching the upper 90s to low \n100s. Precipitation chances remain low, with only modest increases\npossible if a weak boundary or shortwave can influence the region\nlater in the period. Confidence decreases beyond mid next week \nregarding any specific timing of any more substantial pattern \nchange.",
